WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.280
There is a time in every person's life

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.510
when drinking water is deadly.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:08.427
Even as much as a few
ounces is enough to kill.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:18.070
The average healthy adult is
made up of 55 to 60% water.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:22.390
The average baby, on the other
hand, is roughly 75% water.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:25.030
And that difference is why
babies shouldn't drink water

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.520
before they're at least six months old.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.510
Not from the tap or a well or a spring.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.040
Plain water is just plain off limits.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.140
You see, everyone's kidneys have a limit

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.130
to how much water they can handle.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.960
Break that limit, and the excess water

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.780
will back up into your bloodstream,

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.220
where it dilutes the salt,
or sodium, in your blood.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.070
Once your blood dips below 0.4
ounces of sodium per gallon,

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:52.587
you're at risk of a condition
called Hyponatremia.

00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:55.190
It happens when your cells
try to return sodium levels

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.610
to normal by absorbing the extra water

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.350
and swell up like a water
balloon in the process,

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.130
causing complications like confusion,

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:05.560
vomiting and muscle spasms.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.930
Hyponatremia is common in marathon runners

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.730
who drink too much too fast during a race

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.590
without also providing enough sodium

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.740
to balance out their blood.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.270
And if you keep drinking,
that excess water

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.730
will eventually reach
the cells in your brain.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.280
By this point, you have a dangerous case

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.800
of water intoxication, which affects

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.110
roughly 200,000 Americans each year.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.430
It occurs when your brain cells swell,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.010
which builds up pressure inside your skull

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.500
that can lead to seizures, brain damage,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.490
and, in sever cases, death.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.315
But don't worry, dying from
water intoxication

00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:46.300
is extremely hard for
a fully-grown human.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.730
An adult would have to
drink 2.5 to 5 gallons

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.510
every few hours to reach that point.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:55.470
But for newborns, it's a different story.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.550
Their kidneys are about
half the size of an adult's,

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.400
so they can't hold much
water to begin with.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.460
And it takes just a few
ounces to cause problems.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.770
On top of that, their kidneys
aren't developed enough yet

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.730
to properly filter water, so any water

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.340
that enters their body ends
up in the circulatory system,

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.810
where it dilutes their blood

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.730
and increases their
water content by 7 to 8%.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.290
But it's not just drinking straight H2O

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:24.920
that poses a threat.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.870
In fact, most cases of water
intoxication in infants

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.440
don't even involve a glass of water.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.310
A common mistake is when
people dilute baby formula

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.010
too much by accident, or when parents

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.530
dunk their infants up and
down in a swimming pool,

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:43.150
and in the process the infant
gulps in too much water.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.610
It's important that if your baby

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.840
is showing signs of water intoxication

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.690
that you take them to
the hospital immediately,

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.680
where a doctor will likely
provide some form of fluids

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.820
like intravenous saline solution

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.613
to bring the infant's
sodium levels up to normal.

